  "details": "- CVE-2026-14668: make scalarineqsel() verify that a constant it expects to be\n  of type tid actually is\n- CVE-2026-14679: enforce the aggregate argument limit and protect fixed-size\n  FUNC_MAX_ARGS arrays\n- CVE-2026-6464: teach psql to skip in-line data after a COPY ... FROM STDIN\n  that fails before PGRES_COPY_IN, so the data is no longer executed as SQL;\n  such in-line data must now always be terminated by \\.\n- CVE-2026-2006: make the multibyte-to-wchar conversion of every encoding drop\n  an incomplete trailing character, as UTF-8 already did (completes the vendor\n  fix for CVE-2026-2006)\n- pgoutput: report an error instead of crashing the walsender when the\n  proto_version or publication_names option has no value (hardening, no CVE)",
